id: crackling
name: Crackling
kind: conditions
# One stack per clock, so the Square stays Electrified until the last attacker's clock runs
# out rather than the first. The cap only has to be out of anybody's reach, as Ignited's does.
maxStacks: 99
# Not a Combat Condition: the entry makes a Square Electrified and never names one.
combatCondition: no
# The Environmental Quality this mark puts on the Square while it is held. Named here and
# not in the code, where no Quality is named.
quality: electrified
source: Core Rule
description: >
  The ground under you is live. Your Square is Electrified.
text: >
  Crackling: the Elemental (Lightning) Profile's mark. "Any Squares occupied by Character(s)
  who take Damage from this Attacking Maneuver become Electrified (see — Environmental
  Qualities, Battle Environments) until the start of your next turn."

---

# --- The name is this system's ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Ignited's and Frosted's twin: the entry makes a Square Electrified, this system has no
# Squares, and the Environmental Qualities are on the character. So the charge lands on
# whoever took the Damage, as a mark on the attacker's clock, and `qualitiesOf` adds the
# Quality in the `quality:` header while it is held.
#
# Not called Electrified, which is the Quality's own id: one name for two files would have
# the lookup return whichever loaded last.
#
# No effects of its own. What live ground does is the Electrified Quality's file.
